cted -> malformed-input), never from AHE/candidate bytes; it authenticates every lineage candidate through the same chain as the retained cold reopen (openCurrentAnchorTrust from pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest, cut+QC via openCreatorSuccessorTrust, inspectCreatorTrustAdvance, verifySnapshot manifest/payload/state, verifiedCatalog, generation-2 projection, predecessor latched ACL) and additionally requires trust-derived room heads to equal expectedPrevious/expectedNext and epoch+1; it mints no capability and no live material, so it cannot activate. Equivalent same-closure retries are deterministic (sort on encoded generationId, test asserts the published head equals the lexicographically smallest of two genuine Complete generations); already-new is decided by matching an authenticated candidate head before any locator ordering, and the second recovery adds zero swapHead calls; differing authenticated closures fail closed as true-fork; absent/incomplete/wrong-next/malformed cases fail closed. Retained one-call fault custody is preserved by the stageRequestFailed guard, matching the 27-row request-fault expectation (pending-old unless the swap committed). Evidence verified independently: manifest.sha256 is self-excluding and every listed hash (12 source/test paths, plan doc, both reports, ledger) reproduces; focused.json success:true 3/3 with the three current test names; retained.json success:true 86/86, 0 pending, 0 skipped, all statuses passed; 27 stashes present including the named d110c-0b0 exploratory stash; .agents/.claude/.pnpm-store untracked; no provider import or call, no examples/protocol-v3/dependency/threshold/activation/root-export change. Three P2s recorded: the ledger/plan describe the retained run as an eight-file selection while retained.json contains seven result files (numTotalTestSuites 14 = 7 files x 1 describe; the eighth file's 3 tests are proven by focused.json instead), the retained noAheMutationInVerifier governance predicate was narrowed from whole-module to the verifyCreatorSuccessorAdoption slice to admit the co-located mutating recovery kernel, and the fail-closed/decision-model test matrix is thinner than the plan's GREEN bullet. None hides a failure or weakens executed semantics.",
